[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:48. Did You Want to Tell Me Something]
[00:00.500]Passage 48 | 文章四十八
[00:02.920]Did you want to tell me something? | 你想告诉我什么吗？
[00:06.645]Dentists always ask questions when it is impossible for you to answer. | 牙医总是在你无法回答的时候提问。
[00:14.955]My dentist had just pulled out one of my teeth and had told me to rest for a while. | 我的牙医刚拔掉我一颗牙，并告诉我休息一会儿。
[00:22.785]I tried to say something, but my mouth was full of cotton wool. | 我想说些什么，但我的嘴里塞满了棉花。
[00:28.830]He knew I collected birds' eggs and asked me whether my collection was growing. | 他知道我收集鸟蛋，问我收藏品是否在增加。
[00:36.955]He then asked me how my brother was and whether I liked my new job in London. | 接着他问我兄弟怎么样，以及我是否喜欢我在伦敦的新工作。
[00:44.960]In answer to these questions, I either nodded or made strange noises. | 为了回答这些问题，我不是点头就是发出奇怪的声音。
[00:52.960]Meanwhile, my tongue was busy searching out the hole where the tooth had been. | 与此同时，我的舌头忙着寻找那颗牙齿曾经所在的地方。
[01:00.925]I suddenly felt very worried, but could not say anything. | 我突然感到非常担心，但什么也说不出来。
[01:07.335]When the dentist at last removed the cotton wool from my mouth, I was able to tell him that he had pulled out the wrong tooth. | 当牙医最终从我嘴里取出棉花时，我才能够告诉他他拔错了牙。